    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="0882" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg768"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853.015311/2</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Portuguese Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Alte</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic">April 4,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I was very gratified to
                    receive your letter of March 30, 1922, and I beg to thank you most cordially for
                        <pb facs="0883" n="769" xml:id="pg769"/> your kind intervention in the
                    incident occasioned by the hauling down on February 22 of the Portuguese flag
                    flying over the Vice Consulate at Providence, R. I.</p>
                <p>I would esteem it a great favour if you would be good enough to convey to His
                    Excellency the Governor of the State of Rhode Island the assurance that the
                    Portuguese Government and I myself personally deeply appreciated the high sense
                    of international courtesy that inspired his action in this matter.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alte</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
